# Go Standards

## File Header

Every `.go` file must include the package doc comment and copyright:

```go
// Package <name> provides <description>.
//
// Copyright (c) 2025-2026 David Duarte
// Licensed under the MIT License
package <name>
```

## Error Handling

```go
// GOOD — wraps with %w for errors.Is/As support
return fmt.Errorf("failed to create rotor: %w", err)

// BAD — loses error chain
return fmt.Errorf("failed to create rotor: %v", err)
```

- Error strings must be lowercase, no trailing punctuation
- Wrap errors with context: `"failed to <action>: %w"`

## Enigma Components

- Reflectors require **even-sized** alphabets (reciprocal pairs)
- Reflectors must never map a character to itself
- Rotors use `[]int` slices for forward/backward maps (hot path)
- Plugboard currently uses `map[int]int` — prefer slice-based if optimizing
- Always clone components when accepting from external callers

## Imports

Group imports: stdlib, then a blank line, then external packages:

```go
import (
    "fmt"

    "github.com/coredds/enigoma/internal/alphabet"
    "github.com/spf13/cobra"
)
```

## Security Annotations

- `gosec` exclusions G401/G505 are intentional — we simulate historical crypto, not provide real security
- Mark deterministic PRNG usage with `// #nosec G404` comment
